    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148">

                <pb facs="0237" n="215" xml:id="pg215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">399.10–UPU/l–2451:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-01-24T12:00:00+02:00">January 24,
                            1951—noon.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>769. From Redding. France, supporting US position re Chinese Communists but still
                    looks like defeat. France proposes compromise to seat no one and allow
                    Nationalists and Communists participate as observers. Argues this consistent
                    with Security Council action. Request US oppose nominally, asks secret vote.
                    Abstaining governments will support compromise. Argentine now authorized to
                    speak. Please instruct soonest niact.
                    [Redding.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
